        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "To elaborate a bit more:\n\n* it might be a good thing if `__slots__` in a `cdef` class was interpreted as a list of `object` attributes (mainly for pure-Python mode). Although I don't think this is high priority - improvements in Python memory and instance dicts make `__slots__` less useful than before.\n* I think `__slots__` automatically creating a `cdef class` would be a mistake because there's a lot of little ways in which `cdef classes` aren't quite like Python classes.",
            "created_at": "2026-11-15T15:57:25Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/cython/cython/issues/995#issuecomment-6897230755",
            "id": 6897230755,
